---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";
---

<Layout title="MUSU — Distribute AI Coding Tasks Across Your Machines" description="Turn idle computers into an AI workforce. MUSU orchestrates Claude, Gemini, and Codex across your machines. Local-first, zero-config, open source.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="app-layout">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-border pt-12 pb-12">
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-20 -right-14 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-accent/15 blur-3xl" />
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -bottom-24 -left-10 h-52 w-52 rounded-full bg-accent/10 blur-3xl" />

      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.14em] text-text-muted uppercase">AI Operator Layer</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-4xl leading-tight font-bold sm:text-6xl">
        Keep your AI. Add an operator.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Claude, Cursor, GPT. Keep your current workflow.
        MUSU does not replace your tools. It sits underneath and decides
        whether AI changes can actually run.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent">
        Probabilistic AI. Deterministic operation.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a
          class="rounded-full border border-accent bg-accent px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-accent-dim"
          href={SITE.links.windowsDownload}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Download MUSU for Windows (.exe)
        </a>
        <a
          class="rounded-full border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"
          href="/structure"
        >
          See the Structure
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-14 text-center">
      <p class="text-3xl leading-tight font-bold sm:text-5xl">
        AI writes code.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight font-bold text-accent sm:text-5xl">
        MUSU decides if it lives.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xl leading-tight font-semibold text-text-secondary sm:text-3xl">
        Nothing runs without structure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">The problem is not AI.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        AI making mistakes is normal. The real failure is operational:
        no one knows who approved a change, what changed, or why that decision
        was made.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-text-secondary">
        <li>Approval history disappears.</li>
        <li>Diff intent drifts silently.</li>
        <li>Production inherits unstable output.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 font-medium">MUSU structures that operational layer.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Verdict: GO / FIX / BLOCK</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        MUSU does not generate code. It governs acceptance.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-secondary p-4">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-700 dark:text-green-400">GO</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Intent-aligned and executable.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-secondary p-4">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">FIX</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Retry after bounded correction.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-secondary p-4">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-red-700 dark:text-red-400">BLOCK</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-secondary">Boundary violation. Stop immediately.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-text-secondary">
        AI has speed. MUSU adds authority.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Placed beneath your stack</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-secondary p-5">
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{`Your IDE
Your AI
Your Prompt
────────────
MUSU (Operator)
────────────
Execution
State
Production`}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-text-secondary">
        <li>Intent Lock</li>
        <li>Lifecycle Enforcement</li>
        <li>Validation Loop</li>
        <li>Persistent State</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary">
        This is not a framework. It is a running boundary layer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">CPU enforcement layer</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Cloud AI thinks. MUSU watches and enforces. Drift checks, gate decisions,
        and local control run on your machine, so cloud calls are reserved for
        high-value reasoning.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-md border border-border p-4">
          <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.12em] text-text-muted uppercase">Local CPU</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">The enforcer</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Detects out-of-intent changes, validates boundaries, and blocks
            unauthorized execution.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-md border border-border p-4">
          <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.12em] text-text-muted uppercase">Cloud AI</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">The thinker</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Handles complex reasoning and novel generation only when needed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Build vs Run boundary</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Build is generation. Run is operation.
        Production mode is where rollback history, drift monitoring,
        and recovery automation matter.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-medium">MUSU makes that boundary explicit.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-border py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">
        Under your AI. In control of execution.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        You do not need a smarter prompt tool. You need an operator layer that
        makes AI output obey structure before it becomes state.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-semibold">MUSU.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Deep dive</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Want the full mechanism and architecture details?
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          class="rounded-full border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"
          href="/structure"
        >
          Open /structure
        </a>
        <a
          class="rounded-full border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"
          href={SITE.links.docs}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Product Docs
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
